  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fairwinds Technologies has $544M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Fairwinds Technologies won 217 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2.5M and obligations up 6.3% year over year. Fairwinds Technologies received most of its FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $541M. Fairwinds Technologies sells products and services concentrated in electronics manufacturing and related services. Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing accounted for $320M, Other Electronic Component Manufacturing accounted for $136M, and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $79.6M. Fairwinds Technologies also recorded smaller obligations in Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $8.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $500. Fairwinds Technologies had prior fiscal-year activity as well, including $511M in FY25 and smaller totals back to FY21, which helps show the company’s increasing scale in recent years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Fairwinds Technologies' federal obligations?",
        "body": "Fairwinds Technologies' federal obligations are highly concentrated. The Department of Defense obligated $541M of the company’s $544M total in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.2M and the Department of the Interior obligated $30.9K. The Department of Transportation recorded $0 obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and industries drive Fairwinds Technologies' wins?",
        "body": "Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing is the largest market for Fairwinds Technologies at $320M. Other Electronic Component Manufacturing and Other Computer Related Services follow at $136M and $79.6M respectively. Smaller industry obligations include Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $8.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $500."
      }
    ]
  },
